# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Environment variables (keep .env.example, never commit .env)
.env
deploy/**/.env
deploy/**/eval.env

# Deploy kit generated artifacts
deploy/ibm/local-mcp-toolkit/_stage/
deploy/ibm/local-mcp-toolkit/_toolkit.generated.yaml
deploy/**/eval-results/


# IBM Bob IDE directory (skills and MCP tool definition)
.bob/


# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
dist/
/build/

# HB-03b and HB-12 build artifacts: over the task's 5 MB line (18 MB), so they are not committed;
# packs/build/MANIFEST.json records every file's sha256, bytes and row count, and the two
# deliverables beside it are committed.
packs/build/*
# HB-119: the materials resolver's runtime cache (fetched entries only; the committed seed is packs/*.json).
packs/cache/
!packs/build/MANIFEST.json
!packs/build/UNRESOLVED.md
!packs/build/REJECTED_RULES.md

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Ruff
.ruff_cache/

# IDE / editor
.vscode/
.idea/
.zed/
*.swp


# ─── hazbrief-mcp ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# cc_tasks and a session handoff (held privately) are TRACKED (~/GitHub/CLAUDE.md section 6.1, which withdrew the
# BOOTSTRAP-era rule that ignored a session handoff (held privately)). Only data blobs in them are ignored, by size.
# Run logs are local.
logs/
# HB-137 (Issue 594f0f14): an operator tool's runtime state (the display review's pid, log, served record and
# answers). the session state (held privately)'s prior-art ledgers stay tracked; only this subdirectory is local. `serve_review.py stop` copies
# the record into docs/evidence/ for commit.
the session state (held privately)
# HB-141: the live page's recorded operator checks, one JSONL file per serve (orchestrator.yaml web.checks_dir); a
# served brief's runtime state like the review's. `--checks FILE` replays one.
the session state (held privately)
# HB-207 item 1: a live entry form's records (its parse and choice transcripts and the fixture each build writes;
# orchestrator.yaml entry.transcripts_dir and entry.fixtures_dir) are run output, local like the review's. A
# recording kept as a test fixture is copied into docs/evidence/ or fixtures/entry/ and committed.
the session state (held privately)
# Corpus binaries: provenance is url + sha256 in corpus/manifest.yaml (HB-01 rule 2). The
# manifest, the source list, the fetch log and the queue are tracked.
# HB-208: no trailing slash here or on the three graph-data lines below. A dispatched worktree links these
# directories from the primary checkout (symlinks), which a pattern ending in "/" does not match, so they showed as
# untracked and a session's `git status --short` was never empty.
corpus/raw
# Seldon: the Seldon configuration (held privately) and the event log of the graph (held privately) are tracked (the event log is the
# source of truth `seldon rebuild` replays into Neo4j). Local session state is not.
.seldon/
# Operator browser downloads land here unrenamed (DN-002 section 3); scripts/register_inbox.py
# identifies each by content and moves it to corpus/raw/. Never tracked.
corpus/inbox/
# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store
# Squiddy graphs (HB-01b; the corpus graph (held privately)). Mirrors arnold's KG-001 block, which mirrors
# squiddy's own: the ledger, manifest, spec, configs, candidates, text records, decision record
# and evidence records are tracked (the ledger is truth); bulky or local artifacts are not: the
# form-feed text derivatives (regenerable from corpus/raw/), the retrieval index, exports,
# the run's scratch and caches, and the STOP file.
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)
# HB-20: the stopped release's stage-13 export, kept locally for the record; it is an export (above)
# that never sealed, and REPLAY.md rebuilds the released one from the tracked events
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)
# HB-91: squiddy SQ-107's held-file stat cache (revision.STAT_CACHE_NAME): size, mtime and sha256 per held file,
# keyed on the checkout's ABSOLUTE path, rewritten by every build and dry run. Derived, and the kit's own diagnostic
# says to delete it and re-run; committing it would carry one machine's paths and mtimes into every checkout.
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)
the corpus graph (held privately)

# HB-16: the agent eval's per-episode traces (34 MB, over the task's 10 MB line). Each run directory's
# traces_sha256.txt is committed and names every trace by sha256; the ledger, scores, summary,
# progress log and tool surface are committed.
eval/agent_runs/*/claude-*/
# HB-39 (DN-010 D2): the evidence store is the operator's, local; nothing under it is tracked. The committed seed is a
# store of its own, evidence/seed/ (DN-010 s3.4), so the working store never rewrites a tracked file.
evidence/store/
